+# Experimental GPU DMA-BUF transport
+
+`--tp-transport donnerkeule` connects the TP2 executor directly to Donnerkeule's
+four native NHI rails over two USB4 cables. **The standalone verified exchange is currently slower than verbs.** `verbs` remains the default. This is a hardware-qualified
+prototype for fuzzy/misty's gfx1151 / ROCm 7.2.3 setup, not a replacement for
+reliable verbs transport or a production performance improvement.
+
+The final attention/GDN projection and MoE epilogue obtain an output window
+before launch. They write directly into a dedicated HIP TX allocation exported
+as a DMA-BUF. The NHI descriptors address those same pages. The peer NHI writes
+a separate exported HIP RX allocation; the queued GPU consumer reads it and
+adds the local and remote partials into the ordinary residual scratch. Neither
+adapter maps or copies tensor payloads on the CPU, and the old GPU staging copy
+is absent. CPU/GPU control flags remain in a small coherent host allocation.
+
+TX uses cacheable `hipMalloc`; RX uses `hipDeviceMallocUncached` because the
+consumer is already queued behind a GPU wait. A timing-enabled
+`hipEventReleaseToSystem` marker precedes publication of the producer-ready flag.
+This combination is tested on the stated hardware/runtime; do not infer a
+portable external-DMA acquire guarantee for other ROCm versions or GPUs.
+
+## Contract and limitations
+
+- Three 32 MiB windows per direction, dedicated 96 MiB BOs. One stream owns the
+  queue; its producer, publish, wait and consumer run in order. Before a window
+  can be reused, its previous consumer has completed on that stream.
+- TCP exchanges only topology and scope/ordinal/size/readiness records. It never
+  carries tensor data. Physical domain/host IDs and HopIDs pair reversed host
+  enumeration. Four rails are used by the CLI; the adapter config supports 1–8.
+- Ragged payloads are zero-padded on the GPU to 4096 bytes. Transfers larger than
+  the ring batch limit are divided into at most 512 frames per rail per batch.
+- Scope and shape disagreement fails before TX submission. Any failure aborts
+  and drains DMA before waking all queued GPU waits and freeing pools. No retry,
+  reconnect, arbitrary remote write, or hardware reset recovery is provided.
+- Each used session requires **reloading the module on both peers**. Headerless
+  NHI data frames do not provide a generation barrier between old and new
+  processes. The kernel enforces this lifetime rule.
+- The device requires CAP_SYS_RAWIO and exclusive `gpu_direct=1` operation with
+  verbs disabled. Normal Gufo services must release the GPU/verbs devices before
+  switching modules. Do not install this mode as the ordinary service default.
+- Prefill uses Gufo's existing two-lane schedule at 384 tokens and above.
+  Each lane retains a direct output lease, publishes it, then lets the other
+  lane compute before queuing its wait and sum. At most two partials are in
+  flight; the three-window reuse stays behind the previous GPU consumer on
+  the same stream. Short prefill and decode still wait immediately. HIP graph
+  capture remains disabled under TP2.
+
+The vendored `distributed/tbv_gpu_direct.h` is Donnerkeule's ABI version 1
+`include/tbv_gpu_direct.h`, retained verbatim with its Linux syscall-note
+license. Keep the copies synchronized when the ABI changes.
+
+## Build and run
+
+Build with the existing optional RDMA target and the pinned Nix toolchain:
+
+```sh
+nix develop .#tp2-rdma -c cmake --preset gpu-tp2
+nix develop .#tp2-rdma -c cmake --build --preset gpu-tp2 --target \
+  qwen38_flash_next_transport_probe qwen38_flash_next_tp_batched_probe
+```
+
+With fresh direct-mode modules on both hosts, run the transport probe as a
+process permitted to open `/dev/tbv_gpu_direct` (rank 0 listens):
+
+```sh
+qwen38_flash_next_transport_probe --rank 0 --transport donnerkeule --iterations 128
+qwen38_flash_next_transport_probe --rank 1 --connect RANK0_IP \
+  --transport donnerkeule --iterations 128
+```
+
+Run the same binary with `--transport verbs --rdma-device DEVICE` for a matched
+transport control, using normal verbs modules and an ABI-compatible provider.
+The probe generates payloads directly on the GPU, prewarms every RX cache line,
+queues the consumer before the transfer completes, and independently verifies
+every output word. It tests 4 bytes through 32 MiB minus 64 bytes, including
+ragged sizes and multi-batch transfers. Each shape has eight warm-up exchanges.
+`--mismatch 1` deliberately disagrees about the first logical payload size;
+only the expected collective mismatch counts as a passing negative test.
+
+The model probe accepts `--tp-transport donnerkeule`; ordinary `gufo serve llm`
+accepts the same option alongside its existing TP rank/bootstrap/control options.
+The latter still requires the existing authenticated TP control configuration.
+
+## Retained result, October 3–4, 2026
+
+The matched transport diagnostic includes producer, prewarm, publish/wait,
+consumer and full GPU verification; it is **not DMA-only latency**. Per direction,
+256 measured exchanges per shape, with identical binaries and GPU work on both
+hosts. CPU time is process user + system time per exchange; it excludes CPU work
+charged to interrupt handlers or independent kernel workers.
+
+| Payload | Verbs exchange | Direct exchange | Verbs GB/s | Direct GB/s |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 16 KiB | 43.4 µs | 52.8 µs | 0.377 | 0.310 |
+| 1 MiB | 355.8 µs | 375.0 µs | 2.947 | 2.796 |
+| 4 MiB | 1181.8 µs | 1351.3 µs | 3.549 | 3.104 |
+| 32 MiB − 64 B | 8643.2 µs | 12807.0 µs | 3.882 | 2.620 |
+
+At 1 MiB, direct process CPU time was 964–967 µs versus 710–711 µs:
+about 36% more. CPU occupancy was approximately 2.57–2.58 versus 2.0 cores per
+process in this diagnostic. GPU utilization was not measured. Earlier 128-run
+cohorts measured 366 → 410 µs and CPU +40–42%; retain the variability instead of
+claiming a precise invariant penalty. Cacheable TX improved some shapes over
+uncached TX. A separate fine-grained RX trial passed correctness but gave no
+consistent speed gain (1 MiB 389 µs, 4 MiB 1292 µs); it was rejected.
+
+The final direct cohort verified 12,548,983,392 payload bytes per direction with
+zero mismatches, including rotating windows and chunks larger than 8 MiB.
+A deliberate shape mismatch stopped both ranks before TX, with zero payload
+bytes and no hanging GPU wait. The final transport and model builds use
+`c15a6234` plus this change and the same pinned Nix toolchain. Earlier 128-run
+transport logs retain their original `6ddc7cc2` provenance.
+
+The full Q8 model smoke prefills two synthetic 2048-token prompts. All logits
+hashes, generated tokens and active-member transitions match bit for bit between
+both ranks and both transports. The first direct adapter took 4.948 s versus
+4.157 s for verbs. Enabling
+two-lane direct prefill reduced the same 4096-token smoke to 3.941 s; a fresh
+old-build control measured 4.973 s. This isolates a roughly 21% reduction in
+prefill wall time in this diagnostic, with identical full-logit hashes. It is
+not a warmed production speed result or a qualified advantage over verbs.
+Both prompts stopped at
+EOS after only 1 and 3 output tokens, so **this is not a tg128 benchmark**.
+It does not qualify MTP, serving concurrency, images, snapshot replay, or
+upstream model accuracy. A warmed pp2048/tg128 inference comparison and separate
+GPU profiling remain required before any promotion of this backend.
+
+Detailed logs, reproduction metadata and a consistency checker are retained in
+the adjacent Donnerkeule repository under
+`bench/results/2026-10-03-gufo-direct/` and its accompanying report.
+
+## Current checkpoint and next architecture step
+
+The 32K diagnostic (two 32,768-token prompts, context 66,048, eight-token decode
+budget) matches all logit/token signatures on both ranks and transports. Verbs
+prefill takes 59.407 s (1103.2 tokens/s total); direct overlap takes 57.308 s
+(1143.6 tokens/s). The 3.5% difference is a single comparison, not a qualified
+repeatable serving gain. The attempted 64K case never reached prefill: fuzzy's
+model-load threads waited on local NVMe direct I/O while misty exhausted the
+startup barrier. That run was stopped; no 64K timing is claimed.
+
+The empty synchronous barrier now permits 180 seconds for unequal model loads,
+then restores the ordinary 30-second receive deadline. DMA/data deadlines are
+unchanged. The probe adds `--prefill-sweep 4096,32768,65536`: one model load and
+transport lifetime, fresh sessions and a separate scope for each case. It builds,
+but this new multi-case GPU run is not yet verified. All retained model numbers
+above come from the earlier one-case-per-process probe.
+
+Long-term, DMA-BUF MR import, per-NHI DMA mapping and direct descriptors should
+live behind Donnerkeule's verbs operations, including their ordering, completion
+and reliability contract. Keep only transport-neutral producer-output leases,
+GPU visibility and buffer lifetime in Gufo. This migration is recommended, not
+implemented; the separate adapter remains an opt-in reference experiment.
+Normal-mode compatibility of the modified module still needs its own hardware
+check; the existing verbs controls used the saved older module.
+
+The complete checkpoint, machine state and open work are documented in the
+adjacent Donnerkeule repository at `docs/GPU_RDMA_STATUS_2026-10-04.md`.
